Key Achievements:
Nginx Web Server Provisioning: Installed, configured, and managed the Nginx web engine on Ubuntu.

Custom Document Root: Created /var/www/static-site/public and assigned non-root user permissions.

Virtual Host Configuration: Built a custom site block in /etc/nginx/sites-available/static-site and linked it to /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/.

Performance & Security Tuning: Enabled 30-day client-side static asset caching (expires 30d) alongside security headers (X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options).

AWS & Firewall Networking: Allowed inbound HTTP traffic on Port 80 across both UFW and AWS Security Groups.

Technical Architecture & Key Components

| Component           | Setting / Path                          | Purpose / Benefit                                                     |
|---------------------|-----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Web Root            | /var/www/static-site/public             | Isolated directory structure for web files.                           |
| Virtual Host Config | /etc/nginx/sites-available/static-site  | Modular site configuration separated from main Nginx config.          |
| Active Symlink      | /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/static-site    | Enables the site without altering base /etc/nginx/nginx.conf.         |
| Asset Caching       | expires 30d;                            | Forces browser caching for images, CSS, and JS to reduce server load. |
| Security Headers    | X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options | Protects against MIME-sniffing and clickjacking attacks.              

